message: "If you use or reference AI Observatory, please cite this repository."
title: "AI Observatory — Verified AI and Search Crawler Retrieval Monitoring"
version: "1.1.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22850808"
date-released: 2026-09-20

authors:
  - family-names: "Rowley"
    given-names: "Keith"
    affiliation: "Sydney Business Web"

abstract: >
  AI Observatory is a server-side retrieval monitoring framework developed
  by Sydney Business Web. It provides observable evidence of recognised AI
  and search crawler activity using a defined measurement contract that
  separates site attribution, crawler qualification, current business-resource
  retrieval, machine-discovery activity, user-requested retrieval and response
  outcomes. Measurement Contract 1.4 defines 2xx responses as successful
  retrievals, 4xx and 5xx responses as failed retrievals, and 3xx responses as
  neutral evidence excluded from success-rate denominators.

repository-code: "https://github.com/Sydney-Business-Web/ai-observatory"
